+Synthetic aperture radar (SAR)–optical change detectors are usually trained and tested with Sentinel-1 and
+Sentinel-2 images at both dates, but the post-change optical image is often missing or cloudy. We ask
+whether a historical (pre-change) Sentinel-2 image improves Sentinel-1 change detection in that case. On the
+10 test cities of the OSCD urban change benchmark, we evaluate the official dual-stream U-Net (DS-UNet)
+and U-Net baselines with 10 training seeds per model, validation-only selection and an internal pre-
+registration for each step. Within a modality-dropout DS-UNet, removing the historical image made no
+detectable difference (ΔF1 −0.010, 95% CI [−0.026, +0.007]), and at their registered thresholds neither this
+model nor one trained only with SAR and the historical image was detectably better than a SAR-only U-Net.
