 atmospheric effects) and to the DS-UNet configuration studied: there, removing the cloud-affected optical
 pixels and letting a dropout-trained model fall back on bitemporal SAR worked better than passing them
-through. Whether this holds for real cloudy acquisitions, thin cloud, haze or cloud shadow was not tested.
